\DOC DISCHARGE_MEMACCESS_INBOUNDS_TAC

\TYPE {DISCHARGE_MEMACCESS_INBOUNDS_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Closes a goal whose conclusion asserts that a trace of memory-access events
lies within given readable and writable address-range lists.

\DESCRIBE
The tactic takes no arguments. It applies to a goal {A ?- t} where {t} is a
{memaccess_inbounds} claim relating an event trace to two lists of address/size
pairs; the trace may be a literal event list, an {APPEND}/{CONS} combination,
an opaque trace-valued term, or a mixture of these. In the observed traces, the
assumption list typically supplies nonoverlapping facts and
{memaccess_inbounds} facts about sub-traces, and the assumptions are left
untouched.
{
       A ?- t
     ==========  DISCHARGE_MEMACCESS_INBOUNDS_TAC
}

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this closing behaviour, on goals of this single
conclusion form.

\ENDDOC
